source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Serve snouty's run, docs, doctor and settings commands to AI agents over MCP

This command is gated behind the `mcp` unstable feature, because its tools and
their output can still change. Enable it by setting
SNOUTY_UNSTABLE_FEATURES=mcp. An unstable feature can change or go away in any
release.

Starts a Model Context Protocol server on stdin and stdout. An agent starts
`snouty mcp` itself and talks to it over the stdio transport. The server stops
when stdin closes, and the tool calls in progress stop with it.

The tools:
  runs_list        List recent runs
  runs_show        Show details of a specific run
  runs_wait        Wait until a run is ready or complete
  runs_cancel      Cancel a run that has not finished
  runs_properties  List property results for a run
  runs_property    Show one property of a run, by its ID
  runs_build_logs  Stream build logs for a run
  runs_logs        Stream moment logs for a run
  runs_search      Query events with the event-set DSL
  runs_usage       Show the core-hours that recent runs used
  runs_exec        Execute a command in a run that is in progress
  runs_events      Search events in a run
  debug            Launch a debugging session
  docs_tree        Print a tree of documentation paths
  docs_show        Show full contents of a documentation page
  docs_search      Search the documentation
  doctor           Check environment configuration
  version          Print version information
  settings_show    Print the settings that snouty resolved
  tool_help        Return the full help of a tool

Each tool runs its snouty command and returns what the command prints: stdout,
then stderr in a second block when there is any. The output is the text output
of the command, in its detailed form when the command has one. A tool's `json`
param, when true, returns the command's JSON output instead. The params of a
tool are the other arguments of its command, by name. A command that fails marks
the result isError.

A tool call has no time limit and no output limit, and the result arrives only
when the command ends. A call that waits until a run is ready, or that rewarms a
moment, can take minutes. When the client asks for progress, a long call reports
it, so a client that resets its time limit on progress does not end the call.
When the client cancels a call, its command stops. Up to --max-concurrent-calls
tool calls run at the same time.

--settings, --profile and --verbose, and the ANTITHESIS_* environment variables,
apply to every tool call as they do for the other commands.

Example, to add snouty to Claude Code:
  claude mcp add snouty -e SNOUTY_UNSTABLE_FEATURES=mcp -- snouty mcp

Usage: snouty mcp [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --max-concurrent-calls <MAX_CONCURRENT_CALLS>
          The most tool calls that run at the same time; a call waits for a free
          slot
          
          [default: 8]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
